The Nash-Sutcliffe Efficiency (NSE) is then calculated over the paired peak values:
\deqn{PDIFF = 1 - \frac{\sum_{k=1}^N (Q_{\mathrm{obs}, k} - Q_{\mathrm{sim}, k})^2}{\sum_{k=1}^N (Q_{\mathrm{obs}, k} - \bar{Q}_{\mathrm{obs}})^2}}

